WEBVTT

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:09.230
I can't eat another bite...

00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:25.720
This was supposed to be 
like a summer resort...

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:35.840
Lion's father is amazing, isn't he?

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.850
Indeed.

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:44.350
Is he really human?

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:47.730
Indeed.

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:51.560
Why do people get sleepy when they get hot?

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:53.880
Indeed.

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:56.310
Lunch today was delicious, wasn't it?

00:00:56.870 --> 00:00:58.560
Indeed.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:01.360
Can you do my summer homework for me?

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:02.940
Do it yourself.

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:06.210
Sorry about all of this.

00:01:07.150 --> 00:01:11.050
You came all the way out here and 
the air conditioner is broken.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:15.900
P-Please don't concern 
yourself, Mrs. Yelistratova!

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:19.260
You have such good manners, Yayoi-chan.

00:01:19.260 --> 00:01:21.060
If only Lion could take after you.

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:23.470
Huh? Where did she go?

00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:30.660
She better not have run away to 
avoid doing her homework again.

00:01:30.660 --> 00:01:34.230
Lion went out with Mahiro.

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:35.520
Right, mistress?

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:38.780
Yes. She said something about 
finishing off her free research first.

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:40.990
Is that right?

00:01:40.990 --> 00:01:43.120
But I wonder where they 
could have gone off to?

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:47.160
I think they went to the beach, 
or maybe up the mountain?

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:52.040
They went to the forest.

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:54.950
Faster than usual today.

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:30.830
When Lion was a little girl,

00:03:30.830 --> 00:03:33.860
she was so fragile and quite a crybaby.

00:03:33.860 --> 00:03:37.570
She was a spoiled child who 
wouldn't leave my side.

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:42.700
But at some point while playing in the 
mountains and ocean with my muscle-headed husband,

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:44.820
she turned into a little monkey.

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:48.580
I did more or less try to 
homeschool her myself.

00:03:49.390 --> 00:03:52.370
But the only things she got good 
at were camping and fishing.

00:03:53.050 --> 00:03:55.670
I hope she's not a bother to all of you.

00:03:55.980 --> 00:03:59.570
Not at all. Rather, I would say that...

00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:01.890
Her father was the real handful.

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:02.850
Karin!

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:05.680
Yes, you're right. He was.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:09.060
I assure you I gave that musclehead 
a proper punishment after that.

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:12.230
I won't let that fiasco repeat itself.

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:15.350
Bloodthirst?!

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:16.860
Or so I'd like to believe.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:20.650
But didn't he force you all 
to come here this time?

00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:25.700
Gosh, how can I beat something into 
that meathead's long-term memory?

00:04:26.070 --> 00:04:28.700
No, I wouldn't say he forced us.

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:33.540
Lion! I came here to pick you up!

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:36.810
Now, let's go. Come on! Let's go back home!

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:37.290
No.

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:38.960
Why not?

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:40.500
Your closing ceremony already ended, right?

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:44.050
Your daddy and mommy miss you so so so much!

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:46.140
Well, I do miss mommy.

00:04:46.140 --> 00:04:48.600
Report Card

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:48.600
But I want to stay with everyone a bit longer.

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:52.220
What?! You like your friends 
more than your daddy?!

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:54.690
I have to prepare for the 
school festival, too.

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:55.560
I know!

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:58.680
Then you can invite all 
your friends to the castle!

00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:00.860
We'll prepare all sorts of delicious treats!

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:02.500
Food!

00:05:02.500 --> 00:05:04.340
Carbohydrates! Meat!

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:06.390
What?! Stop this instant, Karen!

00:05:06.390 --> 00:05:09.340
It's a castle complete with 
butlers. Luxe vacances.

00:05:09.340 --> 00:05:11.020
Luxe vacances?

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:15.260
It might be a good idea to 
relax every so often, mistress.

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:17.620
Well, if it's only for a week.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:23.640
I'll stay in the dorms.
I have Foreigner research to do.

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:24.750
That's too bad.

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:29.390
There have been eyewitness reports of what 
may be Foreigners near our castle.

00:05:29.770 --> 00:05:31.040
Really?!

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:32.360
Apparently a number of years ago,

00:05:32.360 --> 00:05:35.840
there was a beast that shone with a 
divine light or something like that.

00:05:35.840 --> 00:05:37.390
Me, me! I'm going!

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:38.940
Look at that.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:41.770
Later.

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:54.120
Who could refuse puppy dog eyes like that?

00:05:56.770 --> 00:05:59.960
I feel very sorry for taking 
time away from your parents.

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:03.380
I'm sure they were all looking 
forward to you coming home.

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:06.520
It's just a week, so 
there's no need to worry.

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:07.630
That's right.

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:11.440
All of us have families that 
are very busy with work.

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:13.440
They travel the world non-stop,

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:15.890
so we wouldn't be able to see 
them often just by going home.

00:06:16.240 --> 00:06:20.310
That's why we've decided on days ahead 
of time when we can all get together.

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:24.320
Me too.

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:28.020
It's about the same with my family.

00:06:33.850 --> 00:06:35.700
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:38.210
If you tickle her armpits, she'll let go.

00:06:39.030 --> 00:06:39.990
I see.

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:52.140
Now that you mention it, Mahiro-san 
originally said she'd stay at the dorms.

00:06:55.250 --> 00:07:01.090
My grandpa and grandma and dad 
and mom are all ALCA researchers.

00:07:01.090 --> 00:07:02.600
A family of professors?!

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:06.260
That's not a Foreigner, is it?

00:07:06.260 --> 00:07:07.740
Nope. It's delicious!

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:08.490
Huh?

00:07:11.150 --> 00:07:12.400
Wait!

00:07:15.950 --> 00:07:19.130
Um, we were talking about family, right?

00:07:19.130 --> 00:07:21.270
This might be strange coming from me,

00:07:21.270 --> 00:07:24.220
but they're all completely 
absorbed in their research.

00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:28.110
Even our house in Pirari Town's just
being used as a library now.

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:33.160
I wonder when any of my 
family will come home.

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:38.560
What's the matter? Why'd you suddenly stop?

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:43.060
Um, are you lonely?

00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:46.010
Not at all!

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:48.980
We talk all the time.

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:52.150
Mahiro: It blew up again today!

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:52.150
Mother: A mistake is the key to success!

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:52.150
Father: Mine exploded too.

00:07:48.980 --> 00:07:52.150
Mother: I wonder if it runs in the family...

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:58.090
That's great. My daddy can't even use emoji.

00:08:02.520 --> 00:08:06.280
I'm sure my beloved daughter Lion 
is talking about me right now.

00:08:06.280 --> 00:08:07.420
In a good way.

00:08:11.810 --> 00:08:15.650
Lion's mother is beautiful, isn't she?

00:08:15.650 --> 00:08:18.820
Apparently, she's a former Logicalist.

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:21.350
When did you find that out?

00:08:21.880 --> 00:08:24.920
I happen to be very capable when 
it comes to gathering information.

00:08:24.920 --> 00:08:28.580
Amazing, having a child 
while being a Logicalist.

00:08:31.120 --> 00:08:34.780
Gosh, I won't stand for this, 
even if I should melt from the heat!

00:08:34.780 --> 00:08:37.380
Shall we not do something ourselves?

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:38.120
Do what?

00:08:38.400 --> 00:08:40.240
Something that has meaning!

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:42.310
Like studying or some physical training.

00:08:42.310 --> 00:08:44.180
As students aiming to be Logicalists,

00:08:44.180 --> 00:08:47.400
there is plenty for us to work on.

00:08:51.450 --> 00:08:55.880
Mistress, let's do that after the 
air conditioner has been fixed.

00:09:17.610 --> 00:09:19.900
It doesn't look like there 
are any Foreigners.

00:09:19.900 --> 00:09:22.310
Belle, can you sense anything?

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:26.700
Well, they're not something 
you can find very easily.

00:09:26.700 --> 00:09:29.860
Apparently the Foreigner was 
witnessed a pretty long time ago.

00:09:29.860 --> 00:09:32.710
So there's a pretty big probability 
that it's moved on from here.

00:09:33.200 --> 00:09:35.770
A beast that shone with a divine light...

00:09:37.370 --> 00:09:39.720
Sounds like it might be a Monolium Foreigner.

00:09:43.540 --> 00:09:48.190
I was sure that it'd be Belle's 
father or mother or something.

00:09:48.540 --> 00:09:49.960
Father?!

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:55.730
I had never thought about that before.

00:09:55.730 --> 00:09:57.900
But I guess Bell has a daddy and mommy too.

00:09:58.920 --> 00:10:03.660
Well, who even knows if Foreigners have
an ecosystem like we do here in Septpia?

00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:09.690
We really don't have any idea if Foreigners 
have a similar family system to us,

00:10:09.690 --> 00:10:13.670
or what kind of 
lifestyle they have at all.

00:10:14.160 --> 00:10:15.310
Why not?

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:18.640
It seems from as far back 
as research was conducted,

00:10:18.640 --> 00:10:21.040
ALCA primarily focused on Trancing 
and other such techniques.

00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:22.640
Is that right?

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:25.430
Oh, yeah.  Did you learn 
anything about Belle?

00:10:25.820 --> 00:10:31.440
Yeah! I asked mommy about her and she said 
Belle was her covenanter when she was a Logicalist.

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:37.940
Anything else?

00:10:39.520 --> 00:10:42.280
She said she'll tell me when I get older.

00:10:43.340 --> 00:10:47.720
Well, the principal of our school did give 
you special permission to take her with you.

00:10:47.720 --> 00:10:51.210
So I'm sure she's got some 
sort of special ability.

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:55.420
But looking at her like that, 
she seems like a normal pet.

00:10:56.650 --> 00:10:58.980
To me, she's just another 
member of the family, I guess.

00:10:58.980 --> 00:11:01.800
She's always been with me since I was a baby.

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:02.840
Right, Belle?

00:11:05.670 --> 00:11:08.080
If you could Trance with Belle,

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:10.940
you could see what she really looks like.

00:11:11.320 --> 00:11:12.940
What she really looks like?

00:11:13.680 --> 00:11:16.340
The way Belle looks now 
is like an adaptive body.

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:20.120
It's a form that allows her to 
conform to our world's Logic.

00:11:20.120 --> 00:11:24.450
In Belle's world, she should 
have a much different form.

00:11:24.760 --> 00:11:27.950
Yeah? Can you show me quick, Belle?

00:11:29.260 --> 00:11:30.480
Looks like the answer's no.

00:11:30.480 --> 00:11:31.790
Too bad.

00:11:32.190 --> 00:11:36.870
But, I'd like to go to Belle's world, 
even if just once, to see it.

00:11:36.870 --> 00:11:40.470
If Belle can come here, 
then I can go there, right?

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:50.480
It seems humans don't have adaptive bodies.

00:11:50.860 --> 00:11:52.140
What do you mean?

00:11:55.190 --> 00:11:58.520
Humans can't go to alternate worlds.

00:11:58.520 --> 00:12:00.020
Or so it seems.

00:12:05.580 --> 00:12:07.490
It's a signal from daddy.

00:12:09.460 --> 00:12:11.460
How about we head home?

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:13.440
Fireworks.

00:12:20.890 --> 00:12:22.260
Onee-chan!

00:12:22.580 --> 00:12:24.720
It's time to duel!

00:12:25.220 --> 00:12:28.880
Onee-chan! Onee-chan!

00:12:28.880 --> 00:12:30.970
Yeah, yeah. Later.

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:32.710
Hooray!

00:12:38.200 --> 00:12:40.960
Now this is what I call a luxe vacances.

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:49.920
Karen!

00:12:50.220 --> 00:12:53.750
Now, now. It's shallow, so jumping 
in like that is dangerous.

00:12:54.080 --> 00:12:56.750
Yay! Play with me, mistress!

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:58.630
Wait! I can't breathe!

00:12:58.630 --> 00:12:59.500
Wait!

00:12:59.980 --> 00:13:02.580
Your swimsuit is so cute!

00:13:02.580 --> 00:13:04.510
Put me down this—

00:13:07.630 --> 00:13:10.060
And she's such a child on the inside!

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:11.620
Mistress.

00:13:12.420 --> 00:13:13.820
Do your best.

00:13:13.820 --> 00:13:16.520
At what? What am I doing my 
best to accomplish here?!

00:13:16.910 --> 00:13:20.320
And Karen, how long do you 
intend to hold me up here?

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:22.260
Wait! You can't just throw me—

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:26.570
We're back.

00:13:27.090 --> 00:13:29.570
Wow! A pool!

00:13:30.020 --> 00:13:31.900
Welcome home, Lion.

00:13:31.900 --> 00:13:33.460
It's a pool! A pool!

00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:34.930
Come now.

00:13:34.930 --> 00:13:35.990
This isn't the ocean.

00:13:35.990 --> 00:13:38.060
You have to change into your swimsuit first.

00:13:38.060 --> 00:13:39.480
Okay.

00:13:41.260 --> 00:13:42.500
Mahiro-san.

00:13:42.860 --> 00:13:44.510
Did your journey end in success?

00:13:44.510 --> 00:13:46.620
Naw, it was a bust.

00:13:46.620 --> 00:13:47.970
That's too bad.

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:52.240
But the forest was really pretty.

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:59.350
Monolium might be a world just like that.

00:13:59.720 --> 00:14:02.110
I'd like to see for myself one day.

00:14:02.480 --> 00:14:04.860
Then come with us next time.

00:14:28.170 --> 00:14:30.950
I'm so happy you made so many friends!

00:14:30.950 --> 00:14:33.750
I'm a bit sad, but overjoyed as well.

00:14:33.750 --> 00:14:34.930
Honey.

00:14:35.490 --> 00:14:38.150
Oh, hey honey. Progress is well underway.

00:14:38.150 --> 00:14:40.930
Barbecue preparations are 
going perfectly as well.

00:14:40.930 --> 00:14:43.750
I know the air conditioner is broken,

00:14:43.750 --> 00:14:47.110
but it's still a bit much to build an entire 
pool in half a day for your daughter.

00:14:47.590 --> 00:14:50.110
It was far easier than 
building an entire country.

00:14:50.480 --> 00:14:51.680
You're such a doting father.

00:14:51.680 --> 00:14:54.120
I-I'm also a very devoted husband.

00:14:54.960 --> 00:14:57.110
Goodness. What's the matter, Belle?

00:14:58.240 --> 00:14:59.970
Thank you, Belle.

00:14:59.970 --> 00:15:02.520
I'm happy that you're 
always watching over her.

00:15:03.160 --> 00:15:04.130
Hey, honey.

00:15:04.740 --> 00:15:07.630
Aren't you happy that we sent her to the academy?

00:15:11.600 --> 00:15:16.640
It is a problem that other than her practical exam,
she's getting straight 2s.

00:15:17.110 --> 00:15:21.650
It's all right. That's not really 
 a big problem at all.

00:15:23.330 --> 00:15:24.150
You're right.

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:29.840
I'll take that!

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:36.800
It's so good!

00:15:48.050 --> 00:15:49.240
It's a shooting star!

00:15:49.240 --> 00:15:50.280
I wish I had something good to eat!

00:15:50.280 --> 00:15:52.740
I wish I had—oh, it's already gone.

00:15:52.740 --> 00:15:55.140
You're already eating something good, Karen.

00:15:55.140 --> 00:15:56.350
Now that you mention it,

00:15:56.350 --> 00:15:59.180
the news mentioned that we should be 
able to see a meteor shower today.

00:15:59.540 --> 00:16:00.490
That's right.

00:16:00.490 --> 00:16:04.020
Liones is the best spot 
to see it, latitude-wise.

00:16:04.380 --> 00:16:07.740
Oh. Were you sleeping 
all day today because…

00:16:07.740 --> 00:16:10.280
I was stargazing until early in the morning.

00:16:10.660 --> 00:16:13.280
But apparently, it'll be at its peak today.

00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:17.580
I'd like to see the shooting 
stars tonight, too.

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:19.790
Is there an ideal spot 
where we might see them?

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:22.520
On top of the castle is a good spot.

00:16:22.520 --> 00:16:26.540
But if at all possible, stargazing suits 
an area with few artificial lights best.

00:16:27.020 --> 00:16:29.340
Zhen we doe da best pafs!

00:16:30.510 --> 00:16:31.800
It's not far at all!

00:16:33.730 --> 00:16:36.180
And where exactly is this "not far at all"?

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:37.820
A centipede!

00:16:38.300 --> 00:16:39.420
A ghost!

00:16:43.900 --> 00:16:46.990
Huh? Didn't we go straight last time?

00:16:46.990 --> 00:16:48.400
Don't worry about it.

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:51.400
Are we going somewhere else? Sounds good!

00:17:12.480 --> 00:17:15.510
You like stars a lot, don't you, Nina-chan?

00:17:15.900 --> 00:17:17.030
I do.

00:17:17.030 --> 00:17:19.720
If I wasn't a Logicalist…

00:17:20.990 --> 00:17:23.760
I might have tried to be an astronomer.

00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:27.620
Do you want to go to that star or something?

00:17:27.620 --> 00:17:28.310
Vega?

00:17:28.700 --> 00:17:29.420
Yeah.

00:17:29.420 --> 00:17:33.350
First of all, I didn't say 
I wanted to be an astronaut.

00:17:33.350 --> 00:17:37.490
Next, Vega is over 25 light 
years away from earth.

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:40.740
But… I'd like to go one day.

00:17:50.270 --> 00:17:53.550
You can wish for everything you 
want with all that, mistress.

00:17:53.550 --> 00:17:57.010
Something delicious! Something 
delicious! Something delicious!

00:17:54.440 --> 00:17:57.010
Money! Money! Money!

00:17:57.600 --> 00:17:59.140
You mustn't ask for too much.

00:17:59.140 --> 00:18:00.440
I want to go.

00:18:02.110 --> 00:18:03.860
I want to go to an alternate world.

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:09.740
I want to go to an alternate world!

00:18:12.400 --> 00:18:14.730
I feel all relieved for some reason.

00:18:17.190 --> 00:18:19.710
I always thought it was strange.

00:18:19.710 --> 00:18:22.100
All these Foreigners came to our world,

00:18:22.100 --> 00:18:26.500
but nobody has a clue about 
how they normally live.

00:18:27.180 --> 00:18:29.330
No matter how many books I read,

00:18:29.330 --> 00:18:32.580
or how much I asked my parents, 
I couldn't figure it out.

00:18:33.220 --> 00:18:35.370
Once I formed my own covenant,

00:18:35.370 --> 00:18:37.680
I asked my partner Foreigner about it.

00:18:37.680 --> 00:18:40.720
But for some reason, she wouldn't 
really give me any answers.

00:18:40.720 --> 00:18:45.140
It may be difficult to express in 
the words we use in this world.

00:18:45.140 --> 00:18:49.680
That's why I've got to go myself and 
see everything with my own eyes.

00:18:50.500 --> 00:18:54.520
When I told my parents that, 
they got really mad at me.

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:56.280
Huh? Why?

00:18:56.760 --> 00:19:00.110
Humans don't have adaptive bodies,

00:19:00.110 --> 00:19:02.530
so going to an alternate world 
would put my life at risk.

00:19:04.270 --> 00:19:08.570
But I think there were people who stepped 
up to the challenge in the past.

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:11.560
There's just no information about it.

00:19:12.170 --> 00:19:13.610
You're right.

00:19:13.610 --> 00:19:17.420
It might have something to do 
with ALCA top secret information.

00:19:18.400 --> 00:19:22.150
Well, I don't want to worry 
my parents right now.

00:19:22.150 --> 00:19:26.930
But, make no mistake, the bulk of 
my research stems from that area.

00:19:27.390 --> 00:19:29.200
So that's it.

00:19:29.200 --> 00:19:32.440
Hey, tell us something 
about alternate worlds.

00:19:34.320 --> 00:19:35.190
You can't?

00:19:41.690 --> 00:19:43.700
Belle can sing?!

00:19:44.290 --> 00:19:47.410
I sing this song a lot so 
maybe she picked it up.

00:19:47.900 --> 00:19:49.120
What kind of song is it?

00:19:49.530 --> 00:19:51.030
Um, it goes like…

00:19:54.400 --> 00:19:58.410
Where is this place?

00:19:58.410 --> 00:20:02.380
A place with differing logic

00:20:02.380 --> 00:20:06.440
Under a sky with stars overhead

00:20:03.080 --> 00:20:05.290
I've never heard this melody before.

00:20:06.020 --> 00:20:07.390
Of course.

00:20:06.440 --> 00:20:10.350
They twinkle unknown to me

00:20:07.750 --> 00:20:10.350
After all, it's said to be 
a song not from Septpia.

00:20:10.680 --> 00:20:11.730
Daddy!

00:20:12.150 --> 00:20:14.010
I brought sleeping bags!

00:20:14.010 --> 00:20:16.150
Let's camp out here tonight.

00:20:16.480 --> 00:20:17.660
Yay!

00:20:17.660 --> 00:20:19.580
W-Wait a second.

00:20:19.580 --> 00:20:22.660
If it's not a song from 
Septpia, where is it from?

00:20:22.660 --> 00:20:23.150
Who knows?

00:20:23.580 --> 00:20:27.410
According to Lion's mother, it's 
a song Rosa used to sing.

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:29.910
Which means it's a song from Monolium?!

00:20:30.450 --> 00:20:32.320
We have to check if that's 
true or not right now!

00:20:32.320 --> 00:20:34.310
Where's your Foreigner Card?

00:20:34.310 --> 00:20:36.980
The teachers told me to leave it at school.

00:20:36.980 --> 00:20:38.120
Mahiro-san.

00:20:38.120 --> 00:20:38.540
Huh?

00:20:39.120 --> 00:20:42.670
Students are not allowed to Trance 
outside of the school grounds.

00:20:43.180 --> 00:20:45.600
No! But I'm so curious!

00:20:45.600 --> 00:20:47.750
Totally completely curious!

00:20:47.750 --> 00:20:50.010
Let's go back to the dorm right now!

00:20:50.010 --> 00:20:50.850
Sure.

00:20:53.480 --> 00:20:58.870
Oh no! Nyet!

00:21:01.840 --> 00:21:03.860
Thank you for having us.

00:21:04.370 --> 00:21:06.540
Be careful on your trip home.

00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:08.620
I wish you'd stay longer.

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:09.980
I don't like this either!

00:21:08.940 --> 00:21:10.870
We'll see each other again soon.

00:21:14.560 --> 00:21:17.880
I have plans to come back to the dorm early.

00:21:20.320 --> 00:21:21.910
Me too.

00:21:21.910 --> 00:21:24.500
I have to prepare for the 
school festival, after all.

00:21:25.320 --> 00:21:28.200
First off, I have to think of what we'll do.

00:21:28.200 --> 00:21:30.390
Oh, I think I know something that'd work.

00:21:31.150 --> 00:21:32.440
What is it?!

00:21:32.440 --> 00:21:34.610
Do you have a good idea?

00:21:34.610 --> 00:21:36.560
It just came to me.

00:21:36.560 --> 00:21:39.010
I'll think it over for when 
we get back to the dorm.

00:21:43.120 --> 00:21:47.000
Bye-bye! See you later!

00:21:47.000 --> 00:21:49.390
Now then, Lion. 
What do you want to do today?

00:21:49.390 --> 00:21:51.070
Go fishing on the ocean?

00:21:51.070 --> 00:21:52.660
A walk in the mountains would be fun too.

00:21:52.660 --> 00:21:55.170
Let's see. What should I choose?

00:21:55.170 --> 00:21:57.420
That's obvious.

00:21:58.140 --> 00:21:59.630
First, you need to do your homework!

00:21:59.950 --> 00:22:01.840
Aww.

00:22:01.840 --> 00:22:06.840
Episode 6

00:22:02.840 --> 00:22:06.840
Sleep Brings up a Hina Well

00:22:31.560 --> 00:22:34.040
It really is great with Lion around.

00:22:34.400 --> 00:22:36.480
Drinks taste a hundred times 
more delicious today than usual!

00:22:36.900 --> 00:22:40.040
I know. Linya, how about 
you join me for a drink?

00:22:40.720 --> 00:22:42.540
You're fine with me, even 
though I'm not a young lady?

00:22:43.360 --> 00:22:43.920
Huh?

00:22:43.950 --> 00:22:45.540
Was your mixer fun?

00:22:46.640 --> 00:22:47.920
Here's your summer greeting cards.

00:22:48.380 --> 00:22:50.380
"To The Silver Grizzly,"

00:22:50.380 --> 00:22:52.950
"Thank you for the invitation 
to that mixer the other day."

00:22:53.120 --> 00:22:55.200
"Next time, I'd like to see some girls 
bursting with youthful energy."

00:22:55.790 --> 00:22:56.410
Or so he says.

00:22:57.790 --> 00:22:59.040
<i>Was that from The Lightning of Kremlin?</i>

00:22:59.290 --> 00:23:01.470
<i>He's so good at figuring out how 
a battle on the war front will go,</i>

00:23:01.470 --> 00:23:03.360
<i>so why can't he figure out how 
battles on the home front go?!</i>

00:23:03.590 --> 00:23:06.640
<i>That's why you're still not married!</i>

00:23:07.090 --> 00:23:10.280
Jeez, those guys are a handful, aren't they?

00:23:11.510 --> 00:23:12.080
Yes.

00:23:12.280 --> 00:23:21.960
Next episode

00:23:13.050 --> 00:23:13.910
How to explain this?

00:23:13.910 --> 00:23:17.660
I heard from Lion's teachers that some of Lion's teachers
were tired of being single...

00:23:17.720 --> 00:23:19.840
I was basically no more than logistical support!

00:23:19.840 --> 00:23:21.940
I did nothing suspicious to speak of!

00:23:23.540 --> 00:23:25.610
Please don't give me that cold look!

00:23:25.690 --> 00:23:28.220
Ever since I met you, you've been the 
only one I've ever thought about!

00:23:28.220 --> 00:23:30.920
I don't know a single woman more 
beautiful and strong as you!

00:23:31.150 --> 00:23:34.010
You're the only woman I'll ever 
have eyes for in my entire life!

00:23:34.770 --> 00:23:37.130
I'm not really feeling jealous or anything.

00:23:37.240 --> 00:23:38.300
Linya...
